      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, i see what you did there with the spirits thing, that's slightly better. but honestly, look at the text—it feels really repetitive. you keep using \"cryptic,\" \"enigmatic,\" and \"Hollows\" in almost every sentence. it's starting to feel like you're just swapping out synonyms to make it look longer, which is exactly what i wanted to avoid.\n\nthe depth score is still way too low for the level design team to use this. can you try one more time? really dig into the actual imagery of the Hollows—maybe the smell of the air, the weird trees, or the actual sound of the whispers. i need it to be meaty and long enough to satisfy the engine, but please, for the love of god, don't just use the same three adjectives over and over. make it actually feel like a real piece of lore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
